g we can work around on the engineering side, we need the certificate.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:59] Alice**: Let's keep it open on the release gate rather than pushing it off the board. I'll chase the certificate process.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 37 slack thread window sign gap channel releas date 2026 09 02 2026 09 02 09 14 evan window defend and smartscreen are both flag the build for pilot tester unsign binari get treat a untrust by default 2026 09 02 10 13 alic is the miss code sign certif the actual blocker here 2026 09 02 10 14 evan yes we still don t have one until we do everi pilot instal is go to trip a warn at best get block outright at worst 2026 09 02 10 16 diana releas blocker 2026 09 02 10 17 bob copi 2026 09 02 1018 evan it stay open a far a i m concern this isn t someth we can work around on the engin side we need the certif 2026 09 02 10 59 alic let s keep it open on the releas gate rather than push it off the board i ll chase the certif process\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"id\": \"4223f88ffbddf892\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27719711789173984, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0767128255596283, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7449938, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 927, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:53\", \"token_count\": 288, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-06\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Docker Image Size Optimization\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-25 09:35] Diana**: @Evan, I just pulled the latest `cipherdoc` image. It's 2.1GB! That's way too big for a local runtime deployment. Reopening the Docker packaging task.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 09:30] Evan**: Whoa, 2.1GB, and we still haven't closed out the CVE verification either. Looks like the full Ubuntu base is a big part of the bloat. I'll put together a multi-stage build plan targeting somewhere around 450MB.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 09:33] Diana**: That'd get it onto standard dev laptops without eating all the disk space. Let's aim for that.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 10:04] Evan**: Multi-stage build plan is in place. Stripping out the build-time dependencies from the final artifact.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 13:11] Evan**: The multi-stage split alone still leaves the base layer too large. Swapping from `ubuntu:22.04` to `alpine:latest` as the base. Had some issues with `glibc` vs `musl`, but `gcompat` seems to fix it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 15:21] Evan**: Alpine swap didn't get us all the way there either. Just removed the unused OCR and runtime packages we aren't shipping in this build.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:00] Diana**: Checked the size and ran the CVE scan. We're still over the ~450MB target, and the CVE verification is still failing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:10] Evan**: Yeah, not where we need to be yet. There's still fluff in the Python site-packages layer, and I need to chase down what's tripping the CVE scan.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:13] Diana**: Reopened status stands until both the size and the CVE check are clean. I'll keep tracking it against the release checklist.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 06