ds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"be17298264309b61\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.42203918333786594, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.29887149333980856, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70943046, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:06\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-37\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Signing Gap\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 09:14] Evan**: Windows Defender and SmartScreen are both flagging the build for pilot testers — unsigned binaries get treated as untrusted by default.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:13] Alice**: Is the missing code-signing certificate the actual blocker here?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:14] Evan**: Yes. We still don't have one. Until we do, every pilot install is going to trip a warning at best, get blocked outright at worst.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:16] Diana**: Release blocker?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:17] Bob**: Copy.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:18] Evan**: It stays open as far as I'm concerned — this isn't something we can work around on the engineering side, we need the certificate.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:59] Alice**: Let's keep it open on the release gate rather than pushing it off the board. I'll chase the certificate process.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 37 slack thread window sign gap channel releas date 2026 09 02 2026 09 02 09 14 evan window defend and smartscreen are both flag the build for pilot tester unsign binari get treat a untrust by default 2026 09 02 10 13 alic is the miss code sign certif the actual blocker here 2026 09 02 10 14 evan yes we still don t have one until we do everi pilot instal is go to trip a warn at best get block outright at worst 2026 09 02 10 16 diana releas blocker 2026 09 02 10 17 bob copi 2026 09 02 1018 evan it stay open a far a i m concern this isn t someth we can work around on the engin side we need the certif 2026 09 02 10 59 alic let s keep it open on the releas gate rather than push it off the board i ll chase the certif process\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"id\": \"4223f88ffbddf892\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4201964367822215, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.28903040968888793, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7262505, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 927, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:53\", \"token_count\": 288, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Worker Management Decision\\n\\nRetrospective note on the concurrency block confirmed 2026-08-25. For large-scale redaction jobs, the batch API moved from a synchronous blocking loop to an `asyncio`-driven queue: a single producer walks the file system and pushes document tasks, while a fixed pool of async workers pulls from the queue and orchestrates I/O against the redaction engine, built on top of the already-completed multi-threaded worker pool (T026).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Ordering & Race Risk\\n\\nBecause documents vary widely in size, workers finish out of order. When multiple workers append to the same shared results manifest concurrently, writes can interleave and corrupt the JSON structure.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Update: Confirmed I/O Race, Throughput Regression\\n\\nConcurrency testing on 2026-08-25 confirmed the race is real, not just theoretical: under concurrent load, the race condition measurably cuts batch throughput by roughly 10% compared to the expected async speedup, because workers end up retrying/serializing around the corrupted-write recovery path. This is now blocking further rollout of the async scheduler.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nT037 is **Blocked** on resolving the manifest-write race before the async scheduler can be considered production-ready; the throughput regression it causes depends directly on how the T026 worker pool's result-writing is serialized.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 worker manag decis retrospect note on the concurr block confirm 2026 08 25 for larg scale redact job the batch api move from a synchron block loop to an asyncio driven queue a singl produc walk the file system and push document task while a fix pool of async worker pull from the queue and orchestr i o against the redact engin built on top of the alreadi complet multi thread worker pool t026 sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 order race risk becaus document vari wide in size worker finish out of order when multipl worker append to the same share result manifest concurr write can interleav and corrupt the json structur sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 updat confirm i o race throughput regress concurr test on 2026 08 25 confirm the race is real not just theoret under concurr load the race condit measur cut batch throughput by rough 10 compar to the expect async speedup becaus worker end up retri serial around the corrupt write recoveri path this is now block further rollout of the async schedul sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 status t037 is block on resolv the manifest write race befor the async schedul can be consid product readi the throughput regress it caus depend direct on how the t026 worker pool s result write is serial\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"id\": \"188f8e49d969781d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.41427561420733805, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.31468262315334017, \"vector_similarity\": 0.64665926, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1694, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:51\", \"token_count\": 573, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Background: Path Fix Cleared Packaging\\n\\nBackslash path-handling defects that previously broke Windows builds were fixed on 2026-08-10, and a Windows build artifact was successfully produced by 2026-08-12. Packaging itself is no longer the blocker.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Current Blocker: Missing Code-Signing Certificate\\n\\nThe produced build artifact is unsigned, which triggers a SmartScreen warning and Defender flagging the binary as untrusted.\\n\\n- **Impact**: Site IT policies commonly block execution of unsigned/SmartScreen-flagged binaries outright, which would prevent installation on target deployment workstations without a manual security-policy override.\\n\\n- **Root Cause**: No code-signing certificate has been procured or configured in the Windows build pipeline yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Path to Resolution\\n\\nProcuring a code-signing certificate and wiring signing into the release build step is the only remaining item before this clears the T029 Windows compatibility gate — and, by extension, the T011 release checklist, which is holding on this exact signing gap alongside the T005 image slim-down.\\n\\n*Audit Status*: Active. Build produces successfully; signing certificate procurement is the sole open blocker.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 background path fix clear packag backslash path handl defect that previous broke window build were fix on 2026 08 10 and a window build artifact wa success produc by 2026 08 12 packag itself is no longer the blocker sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 current blocker miss code sign certif the produc build artifact is unsign which trigger a smartscreen warn and defend flag the binari a untrust impact site it polici common block execut of unsign smartscreen flag binari outright which would prevent instal on target deploy workstat without a manual secur polici overrid root caus no code sign certif ha been procur or configur in the window build pipelin yet sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 path to resolut procur a code sign certif and wire sign into the releas build step is the onli remain item befor this clear the t029 window compat gate and by extens the t011 releas checklist which is hold on this exact sign gap alongsid the t005 imag slim down audit status activ build produc success sign certif procur is the sole open blocker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"7d9dbdfb5b6d7c2f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4116822867822215, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.28903040968888793, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69787, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1340, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 387, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Opt-Out Behaviour Designed\\n\\nThe CLI and API collect anonymous usage metrics (pages processed, OCR fallback rate) to help tune the detection engine. Setting `CIPHER_TELEMETRY=0`, or the equivalent GUI toggle, is designed to immediately stop all outbound telemetry traffic to the metrics endpoint.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Design-Time Issue Found and Patched: Pending-Queue Leak\\n\\nWhile designing the flag semantics, testing surfaced that the opt-out flag blocked network egress correctly, but the `TelemetryLogger` kept writing event payloads to a local SQLite queue regardless. That meant re-enabling telemetry later would flush the entire backlog accumulated during the opt-out period, including events the user believed were never being recorded. The logger was patched to a no-op backend when opted out, closing that gap before the flag semantics were finalized.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Verification (Retrospective)\\n\\nA network trace on 2026-08-24 confirmed zero outbound telemetry traffic once the opt-out flag is set, closing the CLI-side verification as Completed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Remaining Limitation\\n\\nThe third-party Electron crash reporter (Sentry) has not been audited for whether it independently respects the opt-out environment variable or requires its own disable hook for minidump uploads.\\n\\n*Note*: CLI-side telemetry opt-out is verified. Full privacy compliance for air-gapped/opt-out users cannot be claimed until the Sentry crash-reporter path is audited separately.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 opt out behaviour design the cli and api collect anonym usag metric page process ocr fallback rate to help tune the detect engin set cipher _ telemetri 0 or the equival gui toggl is design to immedi stop all outbound telemetri traffic to the metric endpoint sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 design time issu found and patch pend queue leak while design the flag semant test surfac that the opt out flag block network egress correct but the telemetrylogg kept write event payload to a local sqlite queue regardless that meant re enabl telemetri later would flush the entir backlog accumul dure the opt out period includ event the user believ were never be record the logger wa patch to a no op backend when opt out close that gap befor the flag semant were final sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 verif retrospect a network trace on 2026 08 24 confirm zero outbound telemetri traffic onc the opt out flag is set close the cli side verif a complet sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 remain limit the third parti electron crash report sentri ha not been audit for whether it independ respect the opt out environ variabl or requir it own disabl hook for minidump upload note cli side telemetri opt out is verifi full privaci complianc for air gap opt out user can not be claim until the sentri crash report path is audit separ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"id\": \"c3381a6a564a6c9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4105444484126547, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.30781704201807814, \"vector_similarity\": 0.65024173, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1587, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:54\", \"token_count\": 503, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \" - *Task opened to design the manual-review quarantine workflow for low-confidence OCR.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-18**: Diana - End-to-end quarantine test; 90% threshold still integrating (Active)\\n\\n - *Ran an end-to-end quarantine test exercising the UI and metadata path; confidence-threshold integration remains Active.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"task open to design the manual review quarantin workflow for low confid ocr 2026 09 18 diana end to end quarantin test 90 threshold still integr activ ran an end to end quarantin test exercis the ui and metadata path confid threshold integr remain activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"id\": \"e90e536e6f3595fa\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4053771290960492, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2950004558514989, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6629227, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1286, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:57\", \"token_count\": 609, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Decision\\n\\nThe CLI accepts an explicit `--no-telemetry` flag. When present, it must suppress every outbound telemetry call for that invocation, including startup pings and error reports — not just usage-metric events.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Why \\\"explicit\\\" matters\\n\\nThe flag was deliberately specified as opt-out rather than opt-in-by-default-off, since the goal was to give privacy-sensitive users a clear, discoverable switch rather than relying on a config file most users would never find.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-32\\n\\n# Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2032\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective decision note on the opt-out flag semantics settled 2026-08-20 for CIPH-48 (Telemetry Opt-Out).\\n\\n## Note\\n\\nThis record settles the flag's expected behavior. Confirming that behavior against an actual network trace was a separate verification step and is not part of this decision note.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out decis the cli accept an explicit no telemetri flag when present it must suppress everi outbound telemetri call for that invoc includ startup ping and error report not just usag metric event sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out whi explicit matter the flag wa deliber specifi a opt out rather than opt in by default off sinc the goal wa to give privaci sensit user a clear discover switch rather than reli on a config file most user would never find sourc id src gdoc 32 telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2032 last updat 2026 09 06 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect decis note on the opt out flag semant settl 2026 08 20 for ciph 48 telemetri opt out note this record settl the flag s expect behavior confirm that behavior against an actual network trace wa a separ verif step and is not part of this decis note\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a043428a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"id\": \"af63545a0d15b5f6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3951168032265771, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2791893260379673, \"vector_similarity\": 0.66561425, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a043428a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 947, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:55\", \"token_count\": 416, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-58\\n\\n# Slack Thread: High-DPI Upstream Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Diana**: Bad news on the high-DPI rendering fix. The rotation fix Charlie pushed works for simple cases, but it's completely breaking on documents with nested Form XObjects.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:43] Charlie**: Yeah, I looked into it. The underlying rendering library we're using (`pdf-lib-core`) has a known bug in how it handles coordinates for XObjects when a parent transform is applied.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Alice**: Can we patch it?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:56] Charlie**: No.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:35] Charlie**: It's deep in their C++ core. I've opened an issue with the upstream maintainers, but they haven't responded.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:37] Evan**: We can't wait for an upstream fix if we're hitting the release gate. Can we work around it by flattening the PDFs first?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:51] Charlie**: Flattening might work but it'll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layers.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:29] Alice**: @Diana, @Charlie, let's leave high-DPI rendering blocked for now. We need to decide if we can ship with this limitation or if we need a different rendering library entirely.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:32] Diana**: Agreed. It only affects a small subset of complex documents, but we should document it as a known issue.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 58 slack thread high dpi upstream block channel cipherdoc date 2026 09 10 2026 09 1010 41 diana bad news on the high dpi render fix the rotat fix charli push work for simpl case but it s complet break on document with nest form xobject 2026 09 1010 43 charli yeah i look into it the under render librari we re use pdf lib core ha a known bug in how it handl coordin for xobject when a parent transform is appli 2026 09 1010 55 alic can we patch it 2026 09 1010 56 charli no 2026 09 10 11 35 charli it s deep in their c core i ve open an issu with the upstream maintain but they haven t respond 2026 09 10 11 37 evan we can t wait for an upstream fix if we re hit the releas gate can we work around it by flatten the pdfs first 2026 09 10 11 51 charli flatten might work but it ll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layer 2026 09 10 12 29 alic diana charli let s leav high dpi render block for now we need to decid if we can ship with this limit or if we need a differ render librari entir 2026 09 10 12 32 diana agre it onli affect a small subset of complex document but we should document it a a known issu\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9310f048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"id\": \"72425f09d11fcc84\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3938196182265771, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2791893260379673, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6612903, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9310f048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1371, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:29\", \"token_count\": 414, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-33\\n\\n# Accessibility Findings: Keyboard Pass on Preview\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2033\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-08 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-21)\\n\\nT039 opened as an accessibility audit of UI surfaces. The first concrete step was keyboard navigation on the redaction preview, so reviewers can move through preview controls without a pointing device.\\n\\n## 2026-08-21 keyboard pass\\n\\nDiana exercised keyboard navigation on the preview surfaces and moved the task to Active. A screen-reader trial was planned as a later step in the same audit and is not documented here.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-33\\n\\n# Accessibility Findings: Keyboard Pass on Preview\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2033\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-08 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-21)\\n\\nT039 opened as an accessibility audit of UI surfaces. The first concrete step was keyboard navigation on the redaction preview, so reviewers can move through preview controls without a pointing device.\\n\\n## Supersession\\n\\nOn 2026-08-24 Alice superseded the a11y audit: the completed visual preview overlay overhaul (T023) was judged to already cover the styling and accessibility scope this task tracked. The keyboard-pass finding therefore did not continue as a standalone a11y workstream.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 33 access find keyboard pas on preview owner diana document key doc 2033 last updat 2026 09 08 retrospect cover 2026 08 21 t039 open a an access audit of ui surfac the first concret step wa keyboard navig on the redact preview so review can move through preview control without a point devic 2026 08 21 keyboard pas diana exercis keyboard navig on the preview surfac and move the task to activ a screen reader trial wa plan a a later step in the same audit and is not document here sourc id src gdoc 33 access find keyboard pas on preview owner diana document key doc 2033 last updat 2026 09 08 retrospect cover 2026 08 21 t039 open a an access audit of ui surfac the first concret step wa keyboard navig on the redact preview so review can move through preview control without a point devic supersess on 2026 08 24 alic supersed the a11y audit the complet visual preview overlay overhaul t023 wa judg to alreadi cover the style and access scope this task track the keyboard pas find therefor did not continu a a standalon a11y workstream\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9da74908a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-08-Accessibility-a11y-Audit-Review.md\", \"id\": \"dbbb35710d0c00e8\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3930550370960492, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2950004558514989, \"vector_similarity\": 0.62184906, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-08-Accessibility-a11y-Audit-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9da74908a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-08-Accessibility-a11y-Audit-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-08-Accessibility-a11y-Audit-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 892, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:06\", \"token_count\": 322, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## What was added\\n\\nAn asynchronous scheduler that accepts batch API jobs and dispatches them to worker threads without blocking the request path, building on the multi-threading work already integrated into the batch CLI.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## Design\\n\\nJobs are queued with a job ID returned immediately to the caller; a separate status endpoint reports progress. Workers pull from the same queue used by the multi-threaded batch path.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-31\\n\\n# Engineering Note: Async Job Scheduler\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2031\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-20)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the async job scheduler added 2026-08-20 to the batch API under CIPH-47, for higher throughput under concurrent load.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis note covers the scheduler's implementation and design only. It does not cover any concurrency issues found during later evaluation of the scheduler under load; those are separate from what this note documents.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load what wa ad an asynchron schedul that accept batch api job and dispatch them to worker thread without block the request path build on the multi thread work alreadi integr into the batch cli sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load design job are queu with a job id return immedi to the caller a separ status endpoint report progress worker pull from the same queue use by the multi thread batch path sourc id src gdoc 31 engin note async job schedul owner bob document key doc 2031 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 20 retrospect note on the async job schedul ad 2026 08 20 to the batch api under ciph 47 for higher throughput under concurr load scope this note cover the schedul s implement and design onli it doe not cover ani concurr issu found dure later evalu of the schedul under load those are separ from what this note document\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e90a788a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"id\": \"0081bbcc02cb4f7b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3900070502265771, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2791893260379673, \"vector_similarity\": 0.64858174, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e90a788a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 956, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:48\", \"token_count\": 412, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"data