9-02 10:17] Bob**: Copy.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:18] Evan**: It stays open as far as I'm concerned — this isn't something we can work around on the engineering side, we need the certificate.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:59] Alice**: Let's keep it open on the release gate rather than pushing it off the board. I'll chase the certificate process.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 37 slack thread window sign gap channel releas date 2026 09 02 2026 09 02 09 14 evan window defend and smartscreen are both flag the build for pilot tester unsign binari get treat a untrust by default 2026 09 02 10 13 alic is the miss code sign certif the actual blocker here 2026 09 02 10 14 evan yes we still don t have one until we do everi pilot instal is go to trip a warn at best get block outright at worst 2026 09 02 10 16 diana releas blocker 2026 09 02 10 17 bob copi 2026 09 02 1018 evan it stay open a far a i m concern this isn t someth we can work around on the engin side we need the certif 2026 09 02 10 59 alic let s keep it open on the releas gate rather than push it off the board i ll chase the certif process\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"id\": \"4223f88ffbddf892\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2673406633460375, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05684059049433932, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7585075, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 927, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:53\", \"token_count\": 288, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Background: Path Fix Cleared Packaging\\n\\nBackslash path-handling defects that previously broke Windows builds were fixed on 2026-08-10, and a Windows build artifact was successfully produced by 2026-08-12. Packaging itself is no longer the blocker.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Current Blocker: Missing Code-Signing Certificate\\n\\nThe produced build artifact is unsigned, which triggers a SmartScreen warning and Defender flagging the binary as untrusted.\\n\\n- **Impact**: Site IT policies commonly block execution of unsigned/SmartScreen-flagged binaries outright, which would prevent installation on target deployment workstations without a manual security-policy override.\\n\\n- **Root Cause**: No code-signing certificate has been procured or configured in the Windows build pipeline yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Path to Resolution\\n\\nProcuring a code-signing certificate and wiring signing into the release build step is the only remaining item before this clears the T029 Windows compatibility gate — and, by extension, the T011 release checklist, which is holding on this exact signing gap alongside the T005 image slim-down.\\n\\n*Audit Status*: Active. Build produces successfully; signing certificate pr